// Ground-truth CBOR encodings produced by tari_bor 0.17.3 (the version
// pinned in the template workspace Cargo.lock) over values built with
// tari_template_lib 0.40.1 and the asiri-types crate. Generated by a
// throwaway Rust binary calling tari_bor::encode on each value; the
// encoders in src/cbor.ts and src/args.ts must reproduce these bytes
// exactly, and the decoders in src/model.ts must read them back.
//
// Fixture values:
// - rules: specification_hash [7;32], cap 10000, bond 100, windows
//   5/5/3/5/3/4, approval threshold 2, dispute threshold 3.
// - keys: [1;32] and [2;32] as RistrettoPublicKeyBytes; [3;32] for the
//   Option case. Component: 0x11 repeated 32 times.
// - tender_info_draft: a Draft TenderInfo for the circle above, name
//   "Uyo Shopkeepers Circle", bound, rules as above, rules_hash
//   [8;32], approvers [1;32]/[2;32]/[3;32], every deadline unset,
//   counts zero, no award or records, forfeits zero, no receipt.
//   Note: a None receipt_id is omitted from the encoding entirely,
//   so this array has 22 items, not 23 (measured against the marked
//   fixture below, which carries a receipt and has all 23).
// - tender_info_marked: an Open TenderInfo with distinct values in
//   the tail fields: receipt_resource is the native token resource,
//   forfeit_for_circle 111, forfeit_locked 222, receipt_id the NFT
//   id from u64 7, lock_epoch 11, counts 3 and 2.
// - circle_info: name as above, approvers [1;32]/[2;32], threshold 2,
//   no auditor, tenders [the component], treasury 10000.

